STYLE: A magnificent hand-made toy theatre of printed cardboard, each piece a flat cutout of thick 4 mm card with visible raw brown cut edges. Painted in Chinese charcoal, soft graphite and luminous dry chalk pastel on textured blue-grey cotton rag paper, with coal-dust smudges and broad gentle strokes. Tender, recognizably Chinese faces, restrained human expressions, round brass split pins on articulated puppets. A fictional Chinese-speaking coal-mining town over several decades: worn blue cotton work jackets, simple homes, a pithead wheel, timbered mine entrance, a telescope, and later a planetarium. Palette: coal black #252B30, graphite #4E5962, paper slate #A3ADB4, chalk cream #ECE8DB, faded workwear blue #526C7B, warm ochre #B99159, lamp amber #DFB87C, deep star indigo #24334F, tiny chalk-silver stars #DCE6EA. Contrast the small amber domestic light with an immense indigo star canopy, ending in one warm light on two hands. Beautiful printed-card craft, quiet dignity, familial love and remembered labour.
CONSTRAINTS: No text, writing, lettering, numbers, labels, logos, signatures or watermarks. No national or company emblems. No photographic people, sculpted 3D characters, plastic, glossy finish or anime. No gore or graphic injury. Everything is flat painted card; actual rods, strings, sky, dust and light come from the theatre. A blind father remains alive, dignified, curious and loved. His sight is never magically restored.
Use case: illustration-story.
Image 1 is the selected key art, generated with gpt-image-2.6-sunburst. Preserve its exact charcoal-and-chalk material, palette and character identities. The grown daughter in Image 1, early thirties, low dark bun, cream buttoned blouse, petrol-blue long cardigan, thin rust-red scarf, dark skirt and practical shoes. A FOUR-PART marionette construction sheet, four completely separate card shapes, generous transparent gaps, all at a common drawing scale: (1) HEAD and neck alone, three-quarter profile facing LEFT, a visible brass neck pin near its bottom; (2) BODY WITH LEGS and shoes as one shape, neck to feet, NO head and NO arms, visible brass neck pin and shoulder pins, one long skirt; (3) her LEFT-SIDE tracing arm alone, full sleeve from shoulder brass pin to extended index finger, pointing DOWN-LEFT at rest, tender relaxed hand; (4) her other full sleeved arm alone, shoulder brass pin to an open palm, hanging mostly down. Body tallest in the middle, head upper left, arms separately to the sides. The neck and shoulder pins are structural joints. Exactly four disconnected shapes; no labels, no assembled duplicate, no hands on the body. One isolated front-facing painted-card cutout on a genuinely transparent alpha background, with every gap transparent. No backdrop, sky, shadows, floor beyond the object, rods, strings, frame or lettering. Entire object inside the image with a generous clear margin. Raw brown card cut edge.
